The MIT licence covers this repository's own work: the firmware source, the
web UI, the documentation and the tooling. A licence can only grant rights
over what its author owns, so for the avoidance of doubt:

  1. THIRD-PARTY LIBRARIES are not part of this grant. Dependencies such as
     PsychicHttp, ArduinoJson and the ESP32 Arduino core are fetched at build
     time by PlatformIO and remain under their own licences.

  2. THE ARTOO CONTROLLER PCB is Steve's hardware design (https://artoo.uk).
     This repository contains firmware for that board, not the board design
     itself. Nothing here grants any rights to the hardware.

  3. THE MK4 ASTROMECH DROID is MrBaddeley's design, distributed as paid
     models through his Patreon (https://www.patreon.com/mrbaddeley). This
     repository contains no print files, geometry or other derivatives of
     his work; if you want the droid, support him and get it from him.

Star Wars, R2-D2 and related names and marks belong to Lucasfilm Ltd. This
is a non-commercial fan project by a hobbyist droid builder, with no
